From 523323fa71871584b29a37c3c1e1ba581c033e4b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 09:54:20 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] node: own the mining pool through the RPC service lifecycle

Publish a configured manager in NodeContext during AppInitMain when RPC and the runtime miningpool option are enabled. Remove process-global pool ownership and request-time global option reads; RPC/HTTP handlers retain their own node's manager.

Interrupt new work and drain accepted job/share operations before node dependencies are torn down. Preserve mutex-protected share deduplication and block-submission claims outside cs_main; reject Reset during active operations. Add isolation, runtime switch, concurrency, drain, HTTP routing and restart controls. The default window remains 1000 shares and state remains intentionally in memory.
